# Cursor AI Rules for Brewskey App v3

**IMPORTANT**: Read `PROJECT_CONSTITUTION.md` for complete guidelines. This file contains critical rules that must be followed.

## Critical Rules

### TestID Requirement (MANDATORY)
- **ALWAYS** use `testID` props for components when creating locators in tests
- **NEVER** use text-based locators (`has-text`, `text=`, etc.) or DOM-specific attributes unless absolutely necessary
- When modifying components, ensure they accept and use `testID` props
- When writing tests, use `page.getByTestId('test-id')` instead of `page.locator('text=...')` or `page.locator('button:has-text(...)')`

### TestID Naming Convention
- Use kebab-case: `submit-button`, `login-form`
- Be descriptive: `submit-button-create-location` not just `submit-button`
- Include context: `input-name` not just `name`

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript with strict types
- Use functional components with hooks
- Follow existing patterns in `src/common/` for reusable components
- Use React Query for data fetching
- Use React Hook Form for forms

## File Organization
- Components: `src/components/` (feature-specific) or `src/common/` (reusable)
- Screens: `src/screens/`
- Hooks: `src/hooks/queries/` (React Query) or `src/hooks/context/` (Context)
- Tests: `tests/e2e/` organized by feature

## Testing
- Use Page Object Model pattern (see `tests/fixtures/page-objects.ts`)
- Mock API calls using fixtures in `tests/fixtures/api-mocks.ts`
- Use `autoAuthenticate: true` when auth is not the focus

## When in Doubt
- Check `PROJECT_CONSTITUTION.md` for detailed guidelines
- Follow existing patterns in the codebase
- Prefer consistency over personal preference
